only during developement
// delete the entire db


REMOTE PODMAN DATABASE RESET (DESTRUCTIVE)

WARNING: This permanently deletes every table and all data in the database named by
POSTGRES_DB inside the pbx-nursing-postgres container. Run this on the remote host
from the project directory. It does not delete the Podman volume or other databases.

podman exec pbx-nursing-postgres sh -lc 'dropdb --force --if-exists --username "$POSTGRES_USER" "$POSTGRES_DB" && createdb --username "$POSTGRES_USER" --owner "$POSTGRES_USER" "$POSTGRES_DB"'


SET UP DATABASE SCHEMA FROM A DATABASE CONNECTION STRING

Replace the example value with the complete PostgreSQL connection string. Quoting the
value prevents shell expansion of special characters in the URL. This applies every
pending Drizzle migration to that database.

podman-compose -f podman-compose.yaml build server && podman-compose -f podman-compose.yaml run --rm -e DATABASE_URL='postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE?sslmode=require' server npm run db:migrate
